# Copy this file, don't edit it in place — .env is gitignored, this one isn't.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# Quote every value in single quotes. That second line sources .env as a shell
# script, so an unquoted value gets executed or mangled. For a literal
# apostrophe inside a value, close-escape-reopen: PASS='it'\''s'
#
# In GitHub Actions these come from repository secrets and variables, not from
# this file. evening.yml forwards the six secrets, the two repository
# VARIABLES (SCAN_FEED, SCAN_UNIVERSE), explicitly sets ACCOUNT_EQUITY=2000
# and RISK_PCT=0.5 as versioned production sizing, and forwards
# SCAN_SESSION_DATE from the Run-workflow form's `session` box (the schedule
# guard pins the intended session for an admitted scheduled run),
# SCAN_SEND_EMAIL from its `skip_email` box and the
# --dry-run flag from its `dry_run` box. The legacy intraday.yml and the
# separate morning.yml forward only the Alpaca pair and cannot send email.
# Morning observations need no new subscription or variable. CLAUDE_MODEL,
# MAX_POSITION_PCT and MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS are read locally only.
#
# What an evening run writes: docs/data.json (rewritten every night),
# docs/picks.json (published model plans, schema 2; suggested shares, no fills),
# docs/charts/<TICKER>.png (gitignored), docs/history/ (immutable recovery), and
# docs/evidence/ (deduplicated source frames, reader prompts and exact chart PNGs).
# The compact reader.json and shared reader-observations/ files are derived
# from final canonical bytes, including restamps. They need no credentials or
# new environment variables; deferred browser requests send no private symbols.
# New plans must pass offline provenance verification before either public JSON
# is replaced. No extra provider/model call or new environment variable is needed.
# Input-stage exception evidence is separately retained under input-diagnostics/
# (gitignored, outside docs/), in a unique directory per invocation. The existing
# evening workflow uploads it separately for 30 days, including produced evidence
# on failure paths. It changes no trading decision or environment configuration.
# Known non-session/incomplete-session/preflight exits do not produce a snapshot.
# --dry-run writes data.json, evidence, recovery and charts, mails nothing and
# records no pick. It can still request provider data. For credential-free
# historical work use tools/historical_validation.py with an isolated output
# directory; it blocks sockets and never replaces the current publication.
# The bounded historical acquisition tool also defaults to offline validation.
# Its explicit --acquire path uses only the existing Alpaca pair below after
# frozen-manifest, zero-cost and owner-scoped authorization checks. It is
# separate from production; no new setting, feed change or secret is required.
# The separate historical-input-proof.yml is manual-only and consumes that pair
# only in its real acquisition step. Rehearsal, installation, offline replay and
# encryption receive no provider secrets. The accepted hosted rehearsal used the
# prior checkout. The prospective delivery relation requires reviewed new-code
# evidence and a separate dated release; it does not reopen the rehearsal slot.
# Owner-declared personal use is not provider consent. No new environment
# setting or secret is added. Real dispatch remains blocked; see
# docs/input-truthfulness/2026-09-29-historical-execution.md for the hold.
# See docs/input-truthfulness/2026-09-28-historical-input-proof.md. Do not paste
# keys into a manifest, approval document, issue, PR, log or chat.

# --- Required -------------------------------------------------------------
# The evening/legacy pipeline checks these with preflight() BEFORE requests, so a
# missing one costs nothing, and the message names every missing variable.
# Which are required depends on the run: `evening` needs all six; `evening
# --dry-run` and SCAN_SEND_EMAIL=false drop the two delivery ones. Local
# `intraday` requires delivery variables only when email is enabled; its
# repository workflow forces email off. The separate morning collector uses
# only the Alpaca pair for admitted names; missing credentials are retained
# as unavailable source coverage, never an accepted quote. An empty value
# counts as missing (an unset repository secret arrives as '').

# Alpaca (https://alpaca.markets -> API Keys). Paper or live keys both work:
# only the historical-data client is built, and nothing here places an order.
# The scan reads the consolidated `sip` daily bars with its request window
# held sixteen minutes behind the clock, which is the free plan's route; the
# intraday and morning checks read IEX snapshots and delayed SIP partial-day
# volume. Morning observations retain source timestamps, label IEX single-venue
# coverage and delayed volume, and never establish broker entry clearance.
# `delayed_sip` is a name the bars endpoint refuses.
ALPACA_API_KEY=''
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=''

# Anthropic (https://console.anthropic.com -> API Keys). Needs billing.
# At most MAX_READS (12) chart reads a night, two attempts each.
# The versioned feasible-first selector uses current mechanical/regime, event,
# geometry and whole-share checks, then at most 2 spare A+/A research reads
# (ranked and deterministic session/ticker rotation). No feasible read is
# displaced. Zero feasible names means at most two research reads; an empty
# research pool makes no model calls. Selection is not final order authority.
# Requested names and actual attempts are archived separately, not billed cost.
# A refused credential stops the calls after the first and the night is graded by the
# checklist alone, marked degraded. So does an answer that the credit balance
# is too low: the mail then says to top up the account. Replies reader
# authority refuses keep the checklist grade and earn no ticket, and so does
# an explicit inapplicable discovery-threshold reply, without a retry; such
# refusals degrade the night only past a quarter of the night's reads, when
# none is accepted, or when a refused name would otherwise have been planned.
# No additional model or provider calls.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=''

# Resend (https://resend.com/api-keys). Not needed for --dry-run.
RESEND_API_KEY=''

# Recipients, comma-separated. Until a domain is verified at
# resend.com/domains, Resend delivers only to the address the account is
# registered under, exactly as spelled; the run log diagnoses a refusal and
# corrects a capital letter on the spot.
EMAIL_TO='you@example.com'

# --- Optional locally; production sizing is versioned in evening.yml -----

# Sender. Falls back to onboarding@resend.dev, which Resend delivers only to
# the account owner. Set a verified-domain sender to mail anyone else.
# RESEND_FROM='alerts@yourdomain.com'

# The configured sizing assumptions the plans are computed from -- not a
# balance, settled cash or buying power. Defaults: $10,000, 0.5% risk a trade
# (inside Bonde's 0.25-1% band), 25% of equity in any one name, four open
# model plans. Every ticket's shares are sized at its limit, the highest fill
# it permits, so the quantity keeps the risk budget and the cap at every fill
# it can take; the page's order sheet reads these back beside each ticket.
# The scheduled personal desk instead sets $2,000 and 0.5% in evening.yml:
# $10 base planned risk and a $500 per-name cap before strategy reductions.
# The shared model budget covers reaction and anticipation plans together,
# including conservative commitments for existing occupied model plans.
# Actual settled cash is unknown to the pipeline and must be checked at the broker.
# The browser-only cash/fees preview uses no account API or environment variable;
# entered amounts remain in the tab and never change published model quantities.
# Known cash-takeover exclusions use the versioned primary-source registry in
# knowledge/event-risk.json; this bounded manual evidence is not live news coverage.
# ACCOUNT_EQUITY='10000'
# RISK_PCT='0.5'
# MAX_POSITION_PCT='25'
# MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS='4'

# --- Optional: overriding the data request --------------------------------
# Each raises on a value it does not understand rather than falling back: a
# typo must not quietly change which data the run read.

# Which Alpaca feed the daily bars come from: sip (default) or iex. A feed
# the account may not query aborts the run with FeedNotAuthorizedError
# naming it; a rejected KEY is CredentialsRejectedError, and this is not its
# fix. Set 'iex' to read the free single-venue feed, which needs no hold-back
# and carries a fraction of the consolidated volume.
# SCAN_FEED='sip'

# Which stocks to read: 'directory' (default, and the workflow's setting)
# refreshes Nasdaq's security-type approximation, with no directory price or
# volume gate (4,797 stocks in the archived September 15 snapshot).
# The $3 session-close policy reads actual bars; seeds/explicit names remain exempt.
# Current-session volume is checked by the scans. 'seed' reads data/symbols.txt (228 names) and
# asks nothing of the network. A directory that will not answer falls back to
# its gzip cache under docs/ for up to seven days, then to the seed, and the
# run is marked degraded either way (`universe_cached`).
# SCAN_UNIVERSE='directory'

# Requested XNYS exchange session for a backfill, YYYY-MM-DD. A pinned
# holiday/weekend or unsupported date fails preflight; no date is substituted.
# Unpinned non-session runs skip before providers and preserve the publication.
# Completion is the scheduled exchange close plus a 15-minute buffer.
# The recorded directory timestamp does not establish historical membership.
# Coverage uses intended stocks excluding SPY; below 50% usable session bars
# fails publication, partial coverage degrades it -- except stale frames each
# ending within the 5 sessions before the session evaluated, for at most 1% of
# the intended stocks, which are counted, named with where each ends, and read
# again at every session they missed by the next session's run when it
# publishes. Alpaca bars remain split-adjusted.
# The workflow forwards it from the Run-workflow form's `session` box.
# SCAN_SESSION_DATE='2026-09-10'

# Publish the record without mailing it (the form's `skip_email` box).
# SCAN_SEND_EMAIL='true'

# The grading model. Local only; the workflow always runs the default.
# Direct Sonnet 4.6 receives output_config.format with the shared JSON schema.
# Authority validation still applies. Initial schema compilation may add
# latency/tokens; request v2 does not increase retries, timeout or token ceiling.
# CLAUDE_MODEL='claude-sonnet-4-6'
